  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Cyanide on reduction with DIBAL-H gives aldehyde. Acid halide with rosenmund reduction reaction gives aldehyde. So, all these reaction&nbsp;are correct except benzyl alcohol with oxidation with strong oxidising agents sodium dichromate will give carboxylic acid not the aldehyde.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/2aa1a864-8c40-4b24-b2c7-d25d55aac27f-20e58c8d-1d4f-4fa0-bfcd-5da3b79c6f0f-image.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 119px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
